id=a52sxq_camera_food_libs
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: camera Food mode libraries
author=kusti420
description=Tester report 2026-10-21, reproduced on the test phone: the camera crashes as soon as Food mode opens (SaliencyFoodPhotoMaker initializing thread: "InvalidOperationException: load nativeNode(id: 1900100) fail"). The A52s vendor floating_feature lists food.samsung.v1 in CAMERA_CONFIG_VENDOR_LIB_INFO, so the One UI 9 camera creates SecSaliencyFoodNode, whose native part (libnode-jni.so) dlopens libFoodDetector.camera.samsung.so (FoodDetector_init / processFood). The S26U does not list that node and ships no Food libraries, so the system image had none. Add the A52s stock libFoodDetector.camera.samsung.so and libFood.camera.samsung.so (both only need libOpenCv.camera.samsung.so + libc/libm/liblog/libc++; every OpenCV symbol they import is exported by the system libOpenCv) from the target firmware and list them in public.libraries-camera.samsung.txt like stock A52s, so the camera app's linker namespace may load them.
